{"vid":"kg6OoR1OSzE","source":"kg6OoR1OSzE.en.json3","lang":"en","cues":[{"t":0.4,"txt":"(music playing)"},{"t":5.3,"txt":"[SPEAKER 1] When you were a kid, did you ever lose your"},{"t":8.5,"txt":"parents in a grocery store or public place?"},{"t":12.3,"txt":"Anyone?"},{"t":16,"txt":"Do you remember that feeling of pure fear?"},{"t":21.3,"txt":"Now try to imagine if that fear stretched beyond a few minutes."},{"t":26,"txt":"What if you couldn't find your parents for hours?"},{"t":29,"txt":"What if you were lost for an entire day?"},{"t":35.5,"txt":"That's the best way I can begin to describe how I felt when I"},{"t":39.3,"txt":"was five years old, riding in the back of a police car alone."},{"t":44.5,"txt":"I hadn't done anything wrong, and I wasn't lost."},{"t":47.9,"txt":"I knew exactly where my mom was."},{"t":51.4,"txt":"She was handcuffed to a chair outside of our home,"},{"t":54.5,"txt":"so she couldn't try to stop them when they took me away."},{"t":58.7,"txt":"She hadn't done anything wrong either."},{"t":61.4,"txt":"She had called 911 because her boyfriend was attacking her."},{"t":65.7,"txt":"When the police arrived, they saw the messy home,"},{"t":69.3,"txt":"not much food in the fridge, my hair was matted."},{"t":73.2,"txt":"Within an hour, I was in the back"},{"t":75.5,"txt":"of that police car."},{"t":78,"txt":"That was the day that I entered the U.S. foster care system."},{"t":82.6,"txt":"When I tell people that I was in foster care for over five years,"},{"t":87.1,"txt":"they're often surprised to hear that both my parents are still"},{"t":90.3,"txt":"alive and that foster care was not their choice."},{"t":94.3,"txt":"A common misconception is that foster care is for children"},{"t":97.7,"txt":"who are orphaned or given up."},{"t":100.3,"txt":"This is not the case."},{"t":102.6,"txt":"The vast majority of children in foster care have living parents,"},{"t":107,"txt":"and two-thirds were removed because of neglect."},{"t":111,"txt":"Neglect is a term that is defined differently"},{"t":114,"txt":"in every state, and that is too often a proxy for poverty."},{"t":119.8,"txt":"In the U.S., we often treat"},{"t":122.3,"txt":"poor families quite poorly."},{"t":125.5,"txt":"In other words, we sometimes take"},{"t":127,"txt":"their children away"},{"t":129.8,"txt":"because they didn't have enough money to care for them,"},{"t":132.6,"txt":"and then we turn around and give someone else"},{"t":135.6,"txt":"hundreds or thousands of dollars every month to"},{"t":139.3,"txt":"care for those exact same children."},{"t":143.8,"txt":"So how did we get here?"},{"t":146.4,"txt":"Well,"},{"t":147.8,"txt":"they say the road to hell"},{"t":149.4,"txt":"is paved with good intentions."},{"t":153.4,"txt":"The first major child abuse case"},{"t":155.6,"txt":"was in 1874."},{"t":157.8,"txt":"A little girl in New York named"},{"t":159.3,"txt":"Mary Ellen Wilson was"},{"t":160.8,"txt":"being horrifically abused."},{"t":163.3,"txt":"Her case had to be tried using"},{"t":165.3,"txt":"animal cruelty laws because we"},{"t":167.7,"txt":"did not yet have sufficient laws"},{"t":169.4,"txt":"to protect children."},{"t":172.3,"txt":"That case, and the public outcry"},{"t":174.5,"txt":"it caused,"},{"t":175.3,"txt":"sparked the modern"},{"t":176.4,"txt":"child protection movement."},{"t":178.7,"txt":"The child welfare system was designed in response"},{"t":181.7,"txt":"for children like Mary Ellen to protect them from"},{"t":185.9,"txt":"severe abuse or neglect, for children whose lives"},{"t":190.9,"txt":"would otherwise be in danger."},{"t":194.2,"txt":"For these children, foster care is meant to be"},{"t":197.2,"txt":"a temporary place to stay while the system supports"},{"t":200.8,"txt":"and rehabilitates the parents."},{"t":203.4,"txt":"The goal is to return children home safely as soon as possible."},{"t":209.1,"txt":"Ideally, foster parents are family first,"},{"t":212.4,"txt":"close friends second, and strangers as a last resort."},{"t":218.3,"txt":"Now, what happens in practice often looks quite different."},{"t":224.4,"txt":"I spent five years in non-relative foster care,"},{"t":228.5,"txt":"living with strangers, even though I had"},{"t":231.3,"txt":"several relatives who could have taken me in."},{"t":235.1,"txt":"My aunt tried from the beginning, and it took"},{"t":237.8,"txt":"five years of her fighting the system's bureaucracy"},{"t":241.2,"txt":"to finally bring me home."},{"t":244.2,"txt":"And that failure of the system is not an anomaly."},{"t":248.6,"txt":"Even though federal law mandates that children be placed with"},{"t":252.1,"txt":"relatives first, fewer than"},{"t":253.6,"txt":"one in three actually are."},{"t":257.3,"txt":"And the system also struggled to rehabilitate parents."},{"t":261.4,"txt":"Like the criminal justice system,"},{"t":263.4,"txt":"the child welfare system is far better at"},{"t":266.6,"txt":"separation and punishment than healing and support."},{"t":272.7,"txt":"I have seen this system from nearly every angle,"},{"t":276.9,"txt":"as a child who lived in it,"},{"t":279.1,"txt":"as a professional researcher evaluating it,"},{"t":282.4,"txt":"and as a volunteer trying to navigate it."},{"t":285.9,"txt":"To give you a sense of the scope, on any given day,"},{"t":288.7,"txt":"there are about 400,000 children in foster care."},{"t":295,"txt":"And the research on this is clear."},{"t":298.4,"txt":"Separating a child from their parents is traumatic"},{"t":302.3,"txt":"and causes long-term damage."},{"t":307,"txt":"As experienced foster parent Ursuline Beaver said,"},{"t":311.6,"txt":"\"Once a kid is taken from their parent,"},{"t":314.1,"txt":"if they didn't have an issue"},{"t":315.4,"txt":"before, they got one now.\""},{"t":319.8,"txt":"And it gets worse than that."},{"t":322.3,"txt":"Too often we allow children to be removed from their families"},{"t":327.6,"txt":"mainly because of poverty and then placed in a government-run,"},{"t":332.1,"txt":"taxpayer-funded system that can expose them to"},{"t":335.9,"txt":"equal or greater harm."},{"t":338.6,"txt":"There are higher rates of abuse within foster care than there"},{"t":342.9,"txt":"are in the general public."},{"t":345.1,"txt":"One in four foster youth have PTSD."},{"t":348.6,"txt":"That's double the rate of combat veterans."},{"t":353.9,"txt":"So why do we allow this to continue?"},{"t":359.7,"txt":"One of the main reasons is that the general public doesn't know"},{"t":362.8,"txt":"much about foster care."},{"t":365.1,"txt":"And much of what they think they know is wrong."},{"t":368.9,"txt":"It is not easy to talk about child abuse,"},{"t":372.8,"txt":"addiction, mental illness."},{"t":375.9,"txt":"It is not easy to talk about foster care."},{"t":378.6,"txt":"So often we don't talk about it,"},{"t":381.6,"txt":"And when we do, we usually pretend that"},{"t":384.3,"txt":"it's something that it's not."},{"t":387.5,"txt":"Some of you may have personal experience with foster care."},{"t":392.3,"txt":"Some of you may be learning about foster care for"},{"t":395,"txt":"the first time today."},{"t":397.2,"txt":"Wherever you fall on that spectrum,"},{"t":400.6,"txt":"I am so glad you're here."},{"t":404.5,"txt":"I believe we all need to talk about foster care more,"},{"t":408.7,"txt":"the same way we've learned we need to talk about poverty,"},{"t":412.2,"txt":"homelessness, incarceration,"},{"t":415.1,"txt":"problems we may not have direct experience with,"},{"t":419.3,"txt":"problems that no one person can solve,"},{"t":422.1,"txt":"but that we all bear some responsibility for."},{"t":427.1,"txt":"We need to talk about foster care because"},{"t":429.3,"txt":"inefficiency and harm thrive in silence."},{"t":435.4,"txt":"We need to talk about foster care because"},{"t":437.2,"txt":"we have a responsibility to these children."},{"t":440.1,"txt":"These are our children."},{"t":442.9,"txt":"And because the system often struggles"},{"t":444.8,"txt":"to find and contact relatives,"},{"t":447.4,"txt":"this could be happening to a child in your"},{"t":449.3,"txt":"extended family right now,"},{"t":451.6,"txt":"and you might not know it."},{"t":454.4,"txt":"But this is not just a moral argument."},{"t":457.1,"txt":"When we allow children to be harmed, they grow into"},{"t":460.6,"txt":"adults at increased risk of"},{"t":463.3,"txt":"homelessness, incarceration,"},{"t":466.6,"txt":"sex trafficking, and more."},{"t":471.5,"txt":"This means we all pay the price twice."},{"t":475.6,"txt":"First, when the kids are in foster care, and after, when"},{"t":479.5,"txt":"they disproportionately end up on the streets or incarcerated."},{"t":484.6,"txt":"One in five people who are homeless were"},{"t":487.1,"txt":"once in foster care."},{"t":490,"txt":"Nearly one in five people in US prisons"},{"t":493,"txt":"were once in foster care."},{"t":495.7,"txt":"One in five."},{"t":498.5,"txt":"We need to fundamentally transform the child welfare"},{"t":502.3,"txt":"system, and to do so, we need widespread support."},{"t":506.8,"txt":"Here's what transformation looks like."},{"t":509.1,"txt":"First, children should only enter foster care when"},{"t":512.1,"txt":"necessary, as a last resort."},{"t":515.4,"txt":"We need to treat neglect driven by poverty as a poverty problem,"},{"t":519.2,"txt":"not a parenting problem."},{"t":521.6,"txt":"In many states, that is already law,"},{"t":524.3,"txt":"and we still remove children for being poor."},{"t":528.2,"txt":"Second, when children do enter care,"},{"t":530.9,"txt":"they should be placed in"},{"t":532.3,"txt":"nurturing homes free from abuse."},{"t":535.3,"txt":"I am not saying that all foster homes are bad, but we need to"},{"t":538.9,"txt":"acknowledge that some are, and that needs to be unacceptable."},{"t":544,"txt":"A nationwide shortage of foster homes means that often agencies"},{"t":549.2,"txt":"don't always have the luxury of being selective, and sometimes"},{"t":553.5,"txt":"harmful homes are tolerated."},{"t":556.2,"txt":"If you love children, consider becoming"},{"t":559.3,"txt":"a foster parent."},{"t":561,"txt":"Third, we need to demand that our taxpayer dollars"},{"t":564.3,"txt":"be used to support families instead of separating them."},{"t":567.5,"txt":"Make no mistake, if you pay taxes in the U.S.,"},{"t":571.7,"txt":"you are funding this system."},{"t":574.8,"txt":"Every year, the United"},{"t":576.5,"txt":"States spends over 32"},{"t":578.5,"txt":"billion dollars on child welfare agencies."},{"t":583,"txt":"Imagine if we redirected some of those billions"},{"t":585.8,"txt":"toward keeping families together in the first place."},{"t":592.3,"txt":"Those of you who know me know that I have dedicated"},{"t":596.2,"txt":"my life to fixing this system."},{"t":599.5,"txt":"But I need your help."},{"t":601.5,"txt":"This is not a problem that one person, one organization,"},{"t":605.8,"txt":"or even one law can solve."},{"t":608.6,"txt":"If it were, we would have"},{"t":610.7,"txt":"solved it by now."},{"t":612.9,"txt":"I wish I could give you an easy answer."},{"t":615.4,"txt":"I can't."},{"t":616.9,"txt":"But I do know this:"},{"t":618.6,"txt":"we cannot fix what we cannot talk about."},{"t":622.1,"txt":"We need to come together and wrestle with this problem."},{"t":625.7,"txt":"And so I am asking all of you"},{"t":627.6,"txt":"to talk about foster care"},{"t":629.4,"txt":"to anyone who will listen."},{"t":636,"txt":"When I was five years old, sitting in the back"},{"t":638.4,"txt":"of that police car, I felt terrified and alone."},{"t":644.9,"txt":"But I wasn't alone."},{"t":646.8,"txt":"I had family."},{"t":648.4,"txt":"I had community."},{"t":650.5,"txt":"It took five years before the system allowed them to help me."},{"t":654.8,"txt":"Five years before I went home to my aunt, my family."},{"t":662.5,"txt":"For me, it was five years."},{"t":666.8,"txt":"For some children, it's longer or never."},{"t":671.7,"txt":"It is time we change that."},{"t":675.3,"txt":"Join me."},{"t":676.5,"txt":"Let's talk about foster care."},{"t":679.9,"txt":"Thank you."},{"t":680.8,"txt":"(applause and cheering)"}],"words":[{"t":0.4,"w":"(music"},{"t":0.4,"w":"playing)"},{"t":5.32,"w":"[SPEAKER"},{"t":5.32,"w":"1]"},{"t":5.32,"w":"When"},{"t":5.32,"w":"you"},{"t":5.32,"w":"were"},{"t":5.32,"w":"a"},{"t":5.32,"w":"kid,"},{"t":5.32,"w":"did"},{"t":5.32,"w":"you"},{"t":5.32,"w":"ever"},{"t":5.32,"w":"lose"},{"t":5.32,"w":"your"},{"t":8.52,"w":"parents"},{"t":8.52,"w":"in"},{"t":8.52,"w":"a"},{"t":8.52,"w":"grocery"},{"t":8.52,"w":"store"},{"t":8.52,"w":"or"},{"t":8.52,"w":"public"},{"t":8.52,"w":"place?"},{"t":12.3,"w":"Anyone?"},{"t":16,"w":"Do"},{"t":16,"w":"you"},{"t":16,"w":"remember"},{"t":16,"w":"that"},{"t":16,"w":"feeling"},{"t":16,"w":"of"},{"t":16,"w":"pure"},{"t":16,"w":"fear?"},{"t":21.32,"w":"Now"},{"t":21.32,"w":"try"},{"t":21.32,"w":"to"},{"t":21.32,"w":"imagine"},{"t":21.32,"w":"if"},{"t":21.32,"w":"that"},{"t":21.32,"w":"fear"},{"t":21.32,"w":"stretched"},{"t":21.32,"w":"beyond"},{"t":21.32,"w":"a"},{"t":21.32,"w":"few"},{"t":21.32,"w":"minutes."},{"t":25.96,"w":"What"},{"t":25.96,"w":"if"},{"t":25.96,"w":"you"},{"t":25.96,"w":"couldn't"},{"t":25.96,"w":"find"},{"t":25.96,"w":"your"},{"t":25.96,"w":"parents"},{"t":25.96,"w":"for"},{"t":25.96,"w":"hours?"},{"t":29,"w":"What"},{"t":29,"w":"if"},{"t":29,"w":"you"},{"t":29,"w":"were"},{"t":29,"w":"lost"},{"t":29,"w":"for"},{"t":29,"w":"an"},{"t":29,"w":"entire"},{"t":29,"w":"day?"},{"t":35.5,"w":"That's"},{"t":35.5,"w":"the"},{"t":35.5,"w":"best"},{"t":35.5,"w":"way"},{"t":35.5,"w":"I"},{"t":35.5,"w":"can"},{"t":35.5,"w":"begin"},{"t":35.5,"w":"to"},{"t":35.5,"w":"describe"},{"t":35.5,"w":"how"},{"t":35.5,"w":"I"},{"t":35.5,"w":"felt"},{"t":35.5,"w":"when"},{"t":35.5,"w":"I"},{"t":39.3,"w":"was"},{"t":39.3,"w":"five"},{"t":39.3,"w":"years"},{"t":39.3,"w":"old,"},{"t":39.3,"w":"riding"},{"t":39.3,"w":"in"},{"t":39.3,"w":"the"},{"t":39.3,"w":"back"},{"t":39.3,"w":"of"},{"t":39.3,"w":"a"},{"t":39.3,"